{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"How ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".coloredNeighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relat